From: GenuineMoron <62113798+GenuineMoron@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] HID: asus: wake the keyboard before sending feature reports

The backlight and Fn-lock writes are sent from the driver's worker with
hid_hw_raw_request() and no runtime PM reference. When USB autosuspend is
enabled for an N-KEY keyboard (power/control = auto), the device suspends
shortly after the last key press, and a SET_REPORT sent to it then fails:

  asus 0003:0B05:19B6.0001: Asus failed to set keyboard backlight: -108

The LED class reports the new brightness but the keyboard keeps the old one
until the next key press resumes it, at which point asus_resume() re-sends
the stored level. On a Zephyrus G16 (GU605MI) this broke "backlight off
when idle" (the light stayed on) and brightness changes made with the
touchpad: 15 failures in one session.

Take a runtime PM reference around these writes with hid_hw_power(), as
hidraw does when userspace opens the device. Only the worker paths do this:
asus_kbd_set_report() is also called from the reset_resume callback, which
must not resume the device it is resuming. If the wake fails, the report
is sent anyway, as before.

Tested on a Zephyrus G16 (GU605MI), linux-cachyos 7.3.4, with the keyboard
autosuspended (power/control = auto): four brightness writes through
/sys/class/leds/asus::kbd_backlight each resumed the device and applied,
with no errors, and the keyboard autosuspended again afterwards. The same
sequence on the unpatched module left the keyboard suspended and logged
"-108" four times.

[NOT YET SENT. Before sending: rebase onto hid.git for-next and rebuild,
and replace the line below with your own Signed-off-by (Developer's
Certificate of Origin: real name and the address you send from).]

Signed-off-by: <your name and email>
---
--- a/drivers/hid/hid-asus.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-asus.c
@@ -596,6 +596,27 @@
 				  HID_REQ_SET_REPORT);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Send a feature report from the worker, waking the keyboard first. With USB
+ * autosuspend enabled the keyboard is suspended a moment after the last key
+ * press, and a SET_REPORT sent to it then fails with -ESHUTDOWN: the backlight
+ * keeps its old level until the next key press resumes the device. Take a
+ * runtime PM reference for the transfer, as hidraw does when userspace opens
+ * the device. Only for the worker: the PM callbacks must not resume the
+ * device they are resuming. If the wake fails, send anyway as before.
+ */
+static int asus_kbd_set_report_awake(struct hid_device *hdev, const u8 *buf,
+				     size_t buf_size)
+{
+	int pm = hid_hw_power(hdev, PM_HINT_FULLON);
+	int ret = asus_kbd_set_report(hdev, buf, buf_size);
+
+	if (pm >= 0)
+		hid_hw_power(hdev, PM_HINT_NORMAL);
+
+	return ret;
+}
+
 static int asus_kbd_init(struct hid_device *hdev, u8 report_id)
 {
 	/*
@@ -693,7 +714,7 @@
 	const u8 buf[FEATURE_KBD_REPORT_SIZE] = { FEATURE_KBD_REPORT_ID, 0xd0, 0x4e, !!enabled };
 	int ret;
 
-	ret = asus_kbd_set_report(hdev, buf, sizeof(buf));
+	ret = asus_kbd_set_report_awake(hdev, buf, sizeof(buf));
 	if (ret < 0)
 		hid_err(hdev, "Asus failed to set fn lock: %d\n", ret);
 }
@@ -705,7 +726,7 @@
 	};
 	int ret;
 
-	ret = asus_kbd_set_report(hdev, buf, sizeof(buf));
+	ret = asus_kbd_set_report_awake(hdev, buf, sizeof(buf));
 	if (ret < 0)
 		hid_err(hdev, "Asus failed to set keyboard backlight: %d\n", ret);
 }
